  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "He was a rank five Gu Master who travelled alone and never married, called Vagrant Lone Star by others; his verses mostly portrayed the starry sky, longing for hometown, and a powerless struggle against fate. He rejected pursuit from women and men alike and kept himself apart from mortal affairs. He could not endure the melancholy in his heart, built his final residence on Xing Jiu peak, and ended his life there, leaving poems for later generations.",
      "chapters": [
        550
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master",
        "loc_xing_jiu_peak"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The inheritance opens every seven days as a brief starlight door guarded by insect groups. Inside, the courtyard is built of blue metal in a strange abstract shape that does not match any style of the five regions. Fang Yuan takes the full inheritance left by the courtyard master and learns this identity there.",
      "chapters": [
        550
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "courtyard-inheritance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Du Min Jun was a righteous path Gu Master, so the inheritance is a righteous path inheritance with only one trial. After Fang Yuan leaves, others who enter find only original poems; the Gu worms and Gu recipes are already gone.",
      "chapters": [
        551
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "courtyard-inheritance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_worms",
        "sys_gu_recipe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Among the gains are emotion poetry Gu, used to store emotions and classed with painting idea Gu as a rare wisdom path Gu, plus large numbers of star path Gu worms of many types that basically cover the star path Gu of Northern Plains. He also left a set of recipes he founded: rank one a bit of star Gu, rank two brilliance of two stars Gu, rank three three stars in the sky Gu, rank four four stars cube Gu, and rank five five stars aligned Gu. That set targets star path Gu and raises their effects much like a non-mainstream amplify effect Gu, with higher success rates and common refinement materials.",
      "chapters": [
        550
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "star-gu-and-recipes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_emotion_poetry_gu",
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "gu_amplify_effect_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan judges the recipe thought process unusual and credits Poet Immortal with deep knowledge behind those ideas.",
      "chapters": [
        551
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "star-gu-and-recipes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Later, Fang Yuan merges Du Min Jun’s inheritance into icy drill stardust and values that merge at four immortal essence stones in treasure yellow heaven when testing hair armor.",
      "chapters": [
        712
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "inheritance-merger",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "inh_du_min_jun_inheritance"
      ]
    }
  ],
